Give the native UI a way back to the shell's.

A tablet or a 2in1 can switch from the shell's browser to Chromium's own
from the shell's settings. Switching back needs that settings page, which
the shell is no longer drawing -- and the choice is remembered, so a
restart comes back to the native UI too. The way out has to be inside the
UI the reader is now looking at.

An item above Settings, in the same group, shown when the native UI is
there because someone asked for it and the shell has given the item a
name. The name is also how the shell says it wants the item: a phone,
where the native UI is simply what there is and there is no setting to
come back to, sends none, and neither does a shell that is drawing the
browser itself.

The words come from the shell rather than from generated_resources.grd.
Compiled in, the string came out in English on a Chinese device -- a new
message has no translations until they are supplied, and a product's own
name is not the engine's to translate. Now renaming it or adding a
language does not mean rebuilding the engine.

This also carries the task runner header that
ohos-new-tab-focuses-omnibox.patch needs in the same file. Two patches
adding includes a few lines apart is how the second one ended up with a
hunk that no amount of context would anchor; one block for both is
steadier, and they are never applied apart.

Choosing it does not switch anything here. It closes the menu and tells the
shell, which saves the setting and calls setBrowserChrome itself. The shell
owns that setting -- it is what writes browserChrome at the next launch --
so switching here as well would leave the two disagreeing after a restart.

diff --git a/chrome/app/chrome_command_ids.h b/chrome/app/chrome_command_ids.h
--- a/chrome/app/chrome_command_ids.h
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_command_ids.h
@@ -596,5 +596,17 @@
 // Context Menu submenus
 #define IDC_SPELLCHECK_MENU 57329
 #define IDC_WRITING_DIRECTION_MENU 57328

+// OHOS: back to the shell's browser from Chromium's own UI. Not in the
+// actions framework: it is reachable only from the app menu, on a platform
+// with no other menu bars to carry it.
+//
+// Below COMMAND_ID_FIRST_UNBOUNDED, which every bounded command has to be.
+// The first attempt took one past the highest number in this file, which
+// was 0xE000 exactly -- the start of the app menu's bookmark range, whose
+// members are 0xE000 + a multiple of five. The menu read the item as a
+// bookmark and asked a delegate that only exists once the bookmark
+// submenu has been opened, so hovering the item dereferenced null.
+#define IDC_OHOS_USE_SHELL_UI 57331
+
 // macOS Top-Level Menu Bar containers
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_model.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_model.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_model.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_model.cc
@@ -86,3 +86,6 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_icon_controller.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/bookmark_sub_menu_model.h"
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/ohos/aura_shell_runtime_bridge.h"
+#endif
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_labs/chrome_labs_prefs.h"
@@ -2478,6 +2478,19 @@
 #endif
 #endif

+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // Above Settings and in its group, because it is the same kind of choice
+  // and whoever needs it is looking for where the settings went.
+  static_assert(IDC_OHOS_USE_SHELL_UI < COMMAND_ID_FIRST_UNBOUNDED,
+                "a bounded command must stay below the unbounded range, "
+                "which this menu hands out to bookmarks");
+  const std::u16string shell_ui_label = chrome::ohos::AuraShellUiMenuLabel();
+  if (!shell_ui_label.empty() &&
+      chrome::ohos::IsAuraShellNativeChromeChosen()) {
+    AddItem(IDC_OHOS_USE_SHELL_UI, shell_ui_label);
+  }
+#endif
+
   AddItemWithStringIdAndVectorIcon(
       this, IDC_OPTIONS, IDS_SETTINGS,
       features::IsRoundedIconsEnabled() ? kSettingsIcon : kSettingsMenuOldIcon);
